    "project_template_level_name": "aif-y2-making-predictions-lesson3-choice1-2026 + template",
    "long_instructions": "An animal shelter is building a multiple linear regression mode. They want to predict how many days it will take for an animal to be adopted.\r\n\r\nYour job is to encode three features: the animal’s age (in months), whether it’s been vaccinated, and the type of animal.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n- Read the initial program in `main.py`.\r\n- Encode the `vaccinated` data.\r\n- Add your encoding to the `features` list.\r\n- Run the program to check your work. You should see your encoding as a column in the printed feature matrix.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nRemember that, to implement a binary encoding, you can use conditionals while iterating over rows of data.\r\n\r\n```\r\nvaccinated_encoding = []\r\nfor row in data:\r\n  if row[\"vaccinated\"] == \"yes\":\r\n    # Encode data\r\n  else:\r\n    # Encode data\r\n```",
